<!-- *********************************************************************	-->
<!-- TEI.extensions.ent file for the TEI, where the TEI is to be generated	-->
<!-- by the TEI Pizza Chef at http://www.tei-c.org/pizza.html			-->
<!-- *********************************************************************	-->
<!-- The TEI Pizza Chef settings:						-->
<!-- Generated by selecting: - Mixed base tagset: Prose and Verse		-->
<!-- Toppings: linking, figures, analysis, transcr, textcrit, names/dates	-->
<!-- No entity set chosen as there is a complete entity set given in the 	-->
<!-- extension files.								-->
<!-- Modification files selected: norron.extensions.ent and 			-->
<!-- norron.extensions.dtd							-->
<!-- Generate full DTD pressed 							-->
<!-- *********************************************************************  	-->
<!-- Made for the research group: 						-->
<!-- Editing medieval manuscripts 						-->
<!-- Centre for Advanced Study							-->
<!-- Norway, 2000-2001. 							-->
<!-- Further changed and updated for the Menota project, see			-->		
<!-- http://www.hit.uib.no/menota/, by Tone Merete Bruvik, The HIT Centre,	-->
<!-- see http://www.hit.uib.no/							-->
<!-- Norway, 2001-2002. 							-->
<!-- *********************************************************************	-->
<!-- When changing extension files, please observe:				-->
<!-- Has to be in SGML syntax. 						-->
<!-- Character with hex value grater than 7F is not allowed anywhere in  	-->
<!-- the extension files due to restrictions in the Pizza Chef.   		-->
<!-- Comments can not contain series of hyphens.				-->
<!-- *********************************************************************	-->
<!--										-->
<!-- May 2, 2002 Tone Merete Bruvik: Added encoding from MASTER (see 		-->
<!-- http://www.hcu.ox.ac.uk/TEI/Master/Reference/). The element expform  	-->
<!-- changed to expForm.   							-->
<!--										-->
<!-- March 26, 2002 Tone Merete Bruvik: Characters not yet defined have		-->
<!-- been set to 003F (which is the character question mark).			-->
<!--										-->
<!-- March 22, 2002 Tone Merete Bruvik: Note can not be an element in		-->
<!-- phrase, has to change orig and reg after all.				-->
<!--										-->
<!-- March 15, 2002 Tone Merete Bruvik: Added 'note' to the element class	-->
<!-- phrase, the elements orig and reg need not to be changed here.		-->
<!-- Referring to the parameter entities, instead of expanded elements.		-->
<!--										-->
<!-- March 13, 2002 Tone Merete Bruvik: Some errors in the Pizza Chef		-->
<!-- generator have now been removed, so that the elements orgName, rdg 	-->
<!-- and lem do not have to be redefined here. The entity table is      	-->
<!-- updated so that entities which already are available in Unicode are  	-->
<!-- using these values, entities which are not, have all been set to 		-->
<!-- the value FFFD.								-->
<!--										-->
<!-- May 21, 2001 Tone Merete Bruvik: Modified and added new elements.   	--> 
<!-- Details about the changes are given in connection to declaration.		-->
<!--										-->
<!-- May 21, 2001 Odd Einar Haugen: Added list of entities referring		-->
<!-- to the Unicode standard (for text in header and notes) and 		-->
<!-- Private Use Area (for text in body). 					-->
<!--										-->
<!-- May 30, 2001 Odd Einar Haugen: Added a few supralinear entities.		-->
<!--										-->
<!-- *********************************************************************	-->
<!--										-->
<!-- May 10, 2003 Odd Einar Haugen: Made a complete revision of the list	-->
<!-- of entities, which now conforms to standard ISO entities (HTML 4.0). 	-->
<!-- Entities outside HTML 4.0 have been defined according to the rules		-->
<!-- set out in the Menota handbook (presently in ch. 2.2, 5 and 6 of       	-->
<!-- version 1.0). All entities are defined with reference to Unicode code  	-->
<!-- points in version 3.2 of this standard, including many in the Private  	-->
<!-- Use Area. Combining diacritical marks have been allocated separate		-->
<!-- entity names, which allows for equivalent encodings of many    		-->
<!-- characters. For example, the a with an acute accent may be encoded		-->
<!-- with the standard ISO entity "&aacute;" or as a sequence of an "a"		-->
<!-- and "&combacute;", the latter referring to COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT,		-->
<!-- 0301 in Unicode. Finally, the names of the characters are now  		-->
<!-- Unicode conformant. Characters in the Private Use Area have been		-->
<!-- named in analogy with the Unicode system.                      		-->

<!-- ********************************************************************* 	-->

<!-- List of important entities not covered in ....... -->

<!ENTITY nbsp "&#x00A0;">		<!-- NON-BREAKING SPACE -->

